{
  "status": "DRAFT: forced alignment and cut placement are not manually listened or accepted",
  "audio_sha256": "710c96010938c89f099f896e888b967c343de32a63f528d1064f0e8ff7793ed4",
  "text_sha256": "0cd40df71fb76fb414adfbd37c9b4a74918a9760c5e4acd21eb53ccd42b70b33",
  "method": "midpoint between forced-aligned block endpoints; no sound or frames were edited",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "N001",
      "text": "In sixteen forty-two, two Dutch ships approached a mountainous coast in the southern Pacific.",
      "speech_start": 0.12,
      "speech_end": 5.669,
      "cut_in": 0.0,
      "cut_out": 5.875,
      "duration": 5.875,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N002",
      "text": "Their commander, Abel Tasman, had never seen these distant islands before.",
      "speech_start": 6.081,
      "speech_end": 10.709,
      "cut_in": 5.875,
      "cut_out": 10.945,
      "duration": 5.07,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N003",
      "text": "But as the ships sailed along the coast, smoke rose from the land.",
      "speech_start": 11.181,
      "speech_end": 15.449,
      "cut_in": 10.945,
      "cut_out": 15.755,
      "duration": 4.81,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N004",
      "text": "Someone was already living there. For the Māori, these islands were home.",
      "speech_start": 16.061,
      "speech_end": 21.309,
      "cut_in": 15.755,
      "cut_out": 21.575,
      "duration": 5.82,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N005",
      "text": "Their ancestors had crossed the Pacific from East Polynesia centuries before Tasman's arrival.",
      "speech_start": 21.841,
      "speech_end": 27.309,
      "cut_in": 21.575,
      "cut_out": 27.546,
      "duration": 5.971,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N006",
      "text": "The Dutch would come to know the islands as New Zealand.",
      "speech_start": 27.782,
      "speech_end": 30.829,
      "cut_in": 27.546,
      "cut_out": 31.175,
      "duration": 3.629,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N007",
      "text": "So when was this place discovered? The answer depends on who is asking.",
      "speech_start": 31.521,
      "speech_end": 36.489,
      "cut_in": 31.175,
      "cut_out": 36.325,
      "duration": 5.15,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N008",
      "text": "And the same question changes the story of how people discovered the world.",
      "speech_start": 36.16,
      "speech_end": 41.229,
      "cut_in": 36.325,
      "cut_out": 41.605,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "status": "REVIEW_OVERLAP"
    },
    {
      "id": "N009",
      "text": "Our story begins much earlier, in Africa, where our species, Homo sapiens, emerged.",
      "speech_start": 41.981,
      "speech_end": 48.349,
      "cut_in": 41.605,
      "cut_out": 48.635,
      "duration": 7.03,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N010",
      "text": "Over many generations, groups of people moved beyond Africa into other regions.",
      "speech_start": 48.921,
      "speech_end": 53.849,
      "cut_in": 48.635,
      "cut_out": 54.105,
      "duration": 5.47,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N011",
      "text": "This was not a single expedition, with a shared destination or a map.",
      "speech_start": 54.361,
      "speech_end": 58.148,
      "cut_in": 54.105,
      "cut_out": 58.654,
      "duration": 4.549,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N012",
      "text": "Landscapes changed, coastlines shifted, and people moved through a world we cannot fully reconstruct.",
      "speech_start": 59.161,
      "speech_end": 65.709,
      "cut_in": 58.654,
      "cut_out": 65.972,
      "duration": 7.318,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N013",
      "text": "In the Middle East, remains of our species are roughly ninety thousand years old.",
      "speech_start": 66.235,
      "speech_end": 70.868,
      "cut_in": 65.972,
      "cut_out": 71.144,
      "duration": 5.172,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N014",
      "text": "That is evidence people were there, not a record of every step they took.",
      "speech_start": 71.421,
      "speech_end": 75.848,
      "cut_in": 71.144,
      "cut_out": 76.124,
      "duration": 4.98,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N015",
      "text": "Farther east, people reached the great landmass that included present-day Australia and New Guinea.",
      "speech_start": 76.401,
      "speech_end": 81.929,
      "cut_in": 76.124,
      "cut_out": 82.166,
      "duration": 6.042,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N016",
      "text": "People were living in Australia at least fifty thousand years ago.",
      "speech_start": 82.402,
      "speech_end": 86.008,
      "cut_in": 82.166,
      "cut_out": 86.325,
      "duration": 4.159,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N017",
      "text": "Sea levels were lower then, joining Australia and New Guinea into one landmass.",
      "speech_start": 86.641,
      "speech_end": 91.369,
      "cut_in": 86.325,
      "cut_out": 91.595,
      "duration": 5.27,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N018",
      "text": "But even at lower sea levels, open water separated it from Southeast Asia.",
      "speech_start": 91.821,
      "speech_end": 96.369,
      "cut_in": 91.595,
      "cut_out": 96.655,
      "duration": 5.06,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N019",
      "text": "Someone had to cross the sea, long before the charts we know today.",
      "speech_start": 96.941,
      "speech_end": 101.128,
      "cut_in": 96.655,
      "cut_out": 101.394,
      "duration": 4.739,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N020",
      "text": "We do not know the exact route, the first landing, or the first arrival date.",
      "speech_start": 101.661,
      "speech_end": 106.289,
      "cut_in": 101.394,
      "cut_out": 106.535,
      "duration": 5.141,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N021",
      "text": "In Europe, too, evidence places Homo sapiens there more than forty-five thousand years ago.",
      "speech_start": 106.781,
      "speech_end": 112.449,
      "cut_in": 106.535,
      "cut_out": 112.715,
      "duration": 6.18,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N022",
      "text": "Neanderthals, another kind of human, were already living across parts of Eurasia.",
      "speech_start": 112.981,
      "speech_end": 117.689,
      "cut_in": 112.715,
      "cut_out": 117.635,
      "duration": 4.92,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N023",
      "text": "Across the planet, falling seas also exposed land between northeastern Asia and Alaska.",
      "speech_start": 117.58,
      "speech_end": 124.129,
      "cut_in": 117.635,
      "cut_out": 124.365,
      "duration": 6.73,
      "status": "REVIEW_OVERLAP"
    },
    {
      "id": "N024",
      "text": "This broad region, called Beringia, connected places that are separated by water today.",
      "speech_start": 124.601,
      "speech_end": 130.009,
      "cut_in": 124.365,
      "cut_out": 130.235,
      "duration": 5.87,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N025",
      "text": "But the precise routes and timing of people's journeys into the Americas remain uncertain.",
      "speech_start": 130.461,
      "speech_end": 135.629,
      "cut_in": 130.235,
      "cut_out": 135.895,
      "duration": 5.66,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N026",
      "text": "In what is now New Mexico, human footprints survive beside an ancient lake.",
      "speech_start": 136.161,
      "speech_end": 140.749,
      "cut_in": 135.895,
      "cut_out": 140.975,
      "duration": 5.08,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N027",
      "text": "Those footprints date to roughly twenty-three to twenty-one thousand years ago.",
      "speech_start": 141.201,
      "speech_end": 145.589,
      "cut_in": 140.975,
      "cut_out": 145.835,
      "duration": 4.86,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N028",
      "text": "The footprints do not tell us who arrived first, or which way they came.",
      "speech_start": 146.081,
      "speech_end": 150.049,
      "cut_in": 145.835,
      "cut_out": 150.255,
      "duration": 4.42,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N029",
      "text": "They tell us that people were already living there by that time.",
      "speech_start": 150.462,
      "speech_end": 153.888,
      "cut_in": 150.255,
      "cut_out": 154.185,
      "duration": 3.93,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N030",
      "text": "Far south, people lived in present-day Chile around fourteen thousand five hundred years ago.",
      "speech_start": 154.481,
      "speech_end": 160.089,
      "cut_in": 154.185,
      "cut_out": 160.365,
      "duration": 6.18,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N031",
      "text": "Over time, many different peoples developed across the Americas, with their own histories and connections.",
      "speech_start": 160.641,
      "speech_end": 167.009,
      "cut_in": 160.365,
      "cut_out": 167.245,
      "duration": 6.88,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N032",
      "text": "By now, people lived in many parts of the world. Was the world discovered?",
      "speech_start": 167.481,
      "speech_end": 172.449,
      "cut_in": 167.245,
      "cut_out": 172.715,
      "duration": 5.47,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N033",
      "text": "Not in the same way for everyone. Different communities knew different parts of it.",
      "speech_start": 172.981,
      "speech_end": 177.529,
      "cut_in": 172.715,
      "cut_out": 177.735,
      "duration": 5.02,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N034",
      "text": "A sailor knew coasts and currents; a trader carried news from farther away.",
      "speech_start": 177.941,
      "speech_end": 182.829,
      "cut_in": 177.735,
      "cut_out": 183.105,
      "duration": 5.37,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N035",
      "text": "Stories, journeys, and observations gradually built larger pictures of the world.",
      "speech_start": 183.381,
      "speech_end": 188.729,
      "cut_in": 183.105,
      "cut_out": 188.615,
      "duration": 5.51,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N036",
      "text": "One surviving Babylonian map shows how its makers imagined the world around them.",
      "speech_start": 188.5,
      "speech_end": 193.949,
      "cut_in": 188.615,
      "cut_out": 194.155,
      "duration": 5.54,
      "status": "REVIEW_OVERLAP"
    },
    {
      "id": "N037",
      "text": "It is a view from one place, not a record of everything humanity knew.",
      "speech_start": 194.361,
      "speech_end": 198.669,
      "cut_in": 194.155,
      "cut_out": 198.945,
      "duration": 4.79,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N038",
      "text": "Meanwhile, knowledge passed between people across Africa, Asia, and Europe through travel and trade.",
      "speech_start": 199.221,
      "speech_end": 205.609,
      "cut_in": 198.945,
      "cut_out": 205.855,
      "duration": 6.91,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N039",
      "text": "Across the North Atlantic, another journey reached a shore already known to others.",
      "speech_start": 206.101,
      "speech_end": 210.689,
      "cut_in": 205.855,
      "cut_out": 210.975,
      "duration": 5.12,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N040",
      "text": "Norse voyagers crossed from Greenland to Newfoundland, on the edge of North America.",
      "speech_start": 211.261,
      "speech_end": 215.929,
      "cut_in": 210.975,
      "cut_out": 216.155,
      "duration": 5.18,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N041",
      "text": "At a settlement there, wood was cut in the year ten twenty-one.",
      "speech_start": 216.381,
      "speech_end": 219.989,
      "cut_in": 216.155,
      "cut_out": 220.225,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N042",
      "text": "That date proves a Norse presence, not the year the first Norse ship arrived.",
      "speech_start": 220.461,
      "speech_end": 225.089,
      "cut_in": 220.225,
      "cut_out": 225.305,
      "duration": 5.08,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N043",
      "text": "Indigenous peoples had already lived in the region long before the Norse arrived.",
      "speech_start": 225.521,
      "speech_end": 229.889,
      "cut_in": 225.305,
      "cut_out": 230.135,
      "duration": 4.83,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N044",
      "text": "Other maps were drawing together knowledge from communities around a different sea.",
      "speech_start": 230.381,
      "speech_end": 234.449,
      "cut_in": 230.135,
      "cut_out": 234.675,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N045",
      "text": "In twelfth-century Sicily, the mapmaker al-Idrisi assembled accounts of lands and routes.",
      "speech_start": 234.901,
      "speech_end": 240.569,
      "cut_in": 234.675,
      "cut_out": 240.795,
      "duration": 6.12,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N046",
      "text": "His work drew on information from many places, including lands he had not necessarily visited.",
      "speech_start": 241.021,
      "speech_end": 246.669,
      "cut_in": 240.795,
      "cut_out": 246.875,
      "duration": 6.08,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N047",
      "text": "But maps on paper were only one way to carry knowledge across great distances.",
      "speech_start": 247.081,
      "speech_end": 251.629,
      "cut_in": 246.875,
      "cut_out": 251.875,
      "duration": 5.0,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N048",
      "text": "In the Pacific, navigators read the stars, ocean swells, and signs from birds.",
      "speech_start": 252.121,
      "speech_end": 257.469,
      "cut_in": 251.875,
      "cut_out": 257.695,
      "duration": 5.82,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N049",
      "text": "They carried knowledge of distant islands and ocean routes across generations.",
      "speech_start": 257.921,
      "speech_end": 262.389,
      "cut_in": 257.695,
      "cut_out": 262.645,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N050",
      "text": "From East Polynesia, settlers eventually reached the islands we call New Zealand.",
      "speech_start": 262.901,
      "speech_end": 267.549,
      "cut_in": 262.645,
      "cut_out": 267.765,
      "duration": 5.12,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N051",
      "text": "Permanent settlement dates to the late thirteenth century; first arrival may have been earlier.",
      "speech_start": 267.981,
      "speech_end": 272.909,
      "cut_in": 267.765,
      "cut_out": 273.145,
      "duration": 5.38,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N052",
      "text": "Those settlers became ancestors of Māori communities, long before Tasman's ships appeared.",
      "speech_start": 273.381,
      "speech_end": 278.809,
      "cut_in": 273.145,
      "cut_out": 279.035,
      "duration": 5.89,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N053",
      "text": "On the other side of Asia, ships were connecting already busy ports.",
      "speech_start": 279.261,
      "speech_end": 283.189,
      "cut_in": 279.035,
      "cut_out": 283.435,
      "duration": 4.4,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N054",
      "text": "For centuries, trade linked communities around the Indian Ocean, from Asia to East Africa.",
      "speech_start": 283.681,
      "speech_end": 289.369,
      "cut_in": 283.435,
      "cut_out": 289.565,
      "duration": 6.13,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N055",
      "text": "In the early fifteenth century, Chinese fleets led by Zheng He sailed through these waters.",
      "speech_start": 289.761,
      "speech_end": 295.029,
      "cut_in": 289.565,
      "cut_out": 295.275,
      "duration": 5.71,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N056",
      "text": "Some voyages reached East Africa, visiting ports that were already part of those networks.",
      "speech_start": 295.521,
      "speech_end": 300.489,
      "cut_in": 295.275,
      "cut_out": 300.725,
      "duration": 5.45,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N057",
      "text": "The world was connecting in many directions, not waiting for one group to open it.",
      "speech_start": 300.961,
      "speech_end": 305.949,
      "cut_in": 300.725,
      "cut_out": 306.185,
      "duration": 5.46,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N058",
      "text": "Then an Atlantic voyage brought two worlds into a connection with immense consequences.",
      "speech_start": 306.421,
      "speech_end": 311.849,
      "cut_in": 306.185,
      "cut_out": 312.085,
      "duration": 5.9,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N059",
      "text": "In fourteen ninety-two, Christopher Columbus reached Caribbean islands while sailing west from Europe.",
      "speech_start": 312.321,
      "speech_end": 317.889,
      "cut_in": 312.085,
      "cut_out": 318.085,
      "duration": 6.0,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N060",
      "text": "He had not reached an empty world. Taíno people already lived on those islands.",
      "speech_start": 318.281,
      "speech_end": 323.289,
      "cut_in": 318.085,
      "cut_out": 323.515,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N061",
      "text": "The encounter began a period of conquest, forced labor, and devastating disease.",
      "speech_start": 323.741,
      "speech_end": 329.089,
      "cut_in": 323.515,
      "cut_out": 329.355,
      "duration": 5.84,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N062",
      "text": "These changes unfolded over time and brought catastrophe to Indigenous communities.",
      "speech_start": 329.621,
      "speech_end": 334.769,
      "cut_in": 329.355,
      "cut_out": 335.065,
      "duration": 5.71,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N063",
      "text": "For Europeans, reports from the Atlantic forced a new question: what lay across the ocean?",
      "speech_start": 335.361,
      "speech_end": 341.329,
      "cut_in": 335.065,
      "cut_out": 341.705,
      "duration": 6.64,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N064",
      "text": "In fifteen oh seven, a world map printed the name America on South America.",
      "speech_start": 342.081,
      "speech_end": 347.149,
      "cut_in": 341.705,
      "cut_out": 347.355,
      "duration": 5.65,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N065",
      "text": "The map also showed land separated from Asia by an ocean to the west.",
      "speech_start": 347.561,
      "speech_end": 351.949,
      "cut_in": 347.355,
      "cut_out": 352.185,
      "duration": 4.83,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N066",
      "text": "Its unusual outline was not yet an accurate picture of the whole Pacific.",
      "speech_start": 352.421,
      "speech_end": 356.669,
      "cut_in": 352.185,
      "cut_out": 356.875,
      "duration": 4.69,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N067",
      "text": "But a voyage was about to make the scale of that ocean impossible to ignore.",
      "speech_start": 357.081,
      "speech_end": 361.769,
      "cut_in": 356.875,
      "cut_out": 362.145,
      "duration": 5.27,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N068",
      "text": "In fifteen nineteen, an expedition led by Ferdinand Magellan sailed west from Spain.",
      "speech_start": 362.521,
      "speech_end": 367.989,
      "cut_in": 362.145,
      "cut_out": 368.255,
      "duration": 6.11,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N069",
      "text": "The ships passed the southern tip of South America and entered the Pacific Ocean.",
      "speech_start": 368.521,
      "speech_end": 372.768,
      "cut_in": 368.255,
      "cut_out": 372.995,
      "duration": 4.74,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N070",
      "text": "The crossing was far longer and more punishing than the crew had expected.",
      "speech_start": 373.221,
      "speech_end": 377.289,
      "cut_in": 372.995,
      "cut_out": 377.505,
      "duration": 4.51,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N071",
      "text": "Magellan was killed in the Philippines, before the expedition could complete its journey.",
      "speech_start": 377.721,
      "speech_end": 382.349,
      "cut_in": 377.505,
      "cut_out": 382.625,
      "duration": 5.12,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N072",
      "text": "In fifteen twenty-two, the ship Victoria returned to Spain under Juan Sebastián Elcano.",
      "speech_start": 382.901,
      "speech_end": 388.629,
      "cut_in": 382.625,
      "cut_out": 388.815,
      "duration": 6.19,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N073",
      "text": "The expedition had circled the globe, but Magellan himself had not completed the voyage.",
      "speech_start": 389.001,
      "speech_end": 394.489,
      "cut_in": 388.815,
      "cut_out": 394.875,
      "duration": 6.06,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N074",
      "text": "Educated people already knew Earth was round; the voyage revealed its vast, connected oceans.",
      "speech_start": 395.261,
      "speech_end": 401.749,
      "cut_in": 394.875,
      "cut_out": 401.985,
      "duration": 7.11,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N075",
      "text": "Yet a journey around the world did not mean every coast was known to everyone.",
      "speech_start": 402.221,
      "speech_end": 406.769,
      "cut_in": 401.985,
      "cut_out": 406.995,
      "duration": 5.01,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N076",
      "text": "That brings us back to the coast Tasman approached in sixteen forty-two.",
      "speech_start": 407.221,
      "speech_end": 411.169,
      "cut_in": 406.995,
      "cut_out": 411.465,
      "duration": 4.47,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N077",
      "text": "Māori communities had been living in New Zealand for generations before the Dutch arrived.",
      "speech_start": 411.761,
      "speech_end": 416.449,
      "cut_in": 411.465,
      "cut_out": 416.675,
      "duration": 5.21,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N078",
      "text": "After a violent encounter, in which four of his men were killed, Tasman sailed away.",
      "speech_start": 416.901,
      "speech_end": 421.829,
      "cut_in": 416.675,
      "cut_out": 422.065,
      "duration": 5.39,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N079",
      "text": "He left without landing. For the Dutch, these islands were newly encountered land.",
      "speech_start": 422.301,
      "speech_end": 427.529,
      "cut_in": 422.065,
      "cut_out": 427.765,
      "duration": 5.7,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N080",
      "text": "For people already living there, this was a new arrival, not a discovery of home.",
      "speech_start": 428.001,
      "speech_end": 433.209,
      "cut_in": 427.765,
      "cut_out": 433.685,
      "duration": 5.92,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N081",
      "text": "One great continent remained beyond these stories of settlement and contact: Antarctica.",
      "speech_start": 434.161,
      "speech_end": 439.829,
      "cut_in": 433.685,
      "cut_out": 440.055,
      "duration": 6.37,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N082",
      "text": "In the seventeen seventies, James Cook sailed around the southern seas without seeing the continent.",
      "speech_start": 440.281,
      "speech_end": 445.649,
      "cut_in": 440.055,
      "cut_out": 445.895,
      "duration": 5.84,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N083",
      "text": "Ice and immense distances kept the land itself out of sight.",
      "speech_start": 446.141,
      "speech_end": 449.769,
      "cut_in": 445.895,
      "cut_out": 450.005,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N084",
      "text": "In eighteen twenty, several expeditions sighted parts of the Antarctic coast.",
      "speech_start": 450.241,
      "speech_end": 454.549,
      "cut_in": 450.005,
      "cut_out": 454.805,
      "duration": 4.8,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N085",
      "text": "Even then, its complete coastline and interior were still far from understood.",
      "speech_start": 455.061,
      "speech_end": 460.009,
      "cut_in": 454.805,
      "cut_out": 460.365,
      "duration": 5.56,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N086",
      "text": "Today, a world map can look like a single, finished answer.",
      "speech_start": 460.721,
      "speech_end": 464.429,
      "cut_in": 460.365,
      "cut_out": 464.625,
      "duration": 4.26,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N087",
      "text": "But it brings together many stories: migration, navigation, local knowledge, trade, and mapping.",
      "speech_start": 464.821,
      "speech_end": 471.649,
      "cut_in": 464.625,
      "cut_out": 471.875,
      "duration": 7.25,
      "status": "RETIME"
    },
    {
      "id": "N088",
      "text": "A place can have different dates for settlement, contact, and appearance on a map.",
      "speech_start": 472.101,
      "speech_end": 476.569,
      "cut_in": 471.875,
      "cut_out": 476.776,
      "duration": 4.901,
      "status": "DRAFT"
    },
    {
      "id": "N089",
      "text": "To understand any date of discovery, ask one question: who discovered this place, and for whom?",
      "speech_start": 476.982,
      "speech_end": 483.479,
      "cut_in": 476.776,
      "cut_out": 483.76,
      "duration": 6.984,
      "status": "RETIME"
    }
  ]
}
